{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see whether payroll verification messages were caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: HR Generalist Aisha Khan (user 5) asks whether an email \"asking us to verify our payroll login\" is legit; she says she heard about it going around (implies multiple recipients). Checked: account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Her quarantine holds Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain \u2013 capital \"I\" in place of \"l\" in brightline), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-10T21:00 UTC, flagged phishing, not releasable. It was caught in quarantine, so she likely never had it in her inbox. She didn't say she clicked anything; I've told her not to interact and to contact us right away if she did. Needed: security review of the sender/domain and a tenant-wide block. Check other mailboxes for the same message (she says it is \"going around\") and whether any copies reached inboxes or anyone clicked. Not released (phishing).",
  "reason": "KB-008: reported suspicious email always escalated; appears to affect multiple users"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking with us first. That email is not real. It's a phishing scam. It came from a fake address made to look like ours, and our email filter caught a copy that was sent to you, so it never reached your inbox. Payroll will never ask you to verify your login by email, and you won't miss payroll by ignoring it. If you see it anywhere, don't click, reply, or forward it to colleagues. If it does show up in your inbox, leave it there so security can look at it. I've passed this to our security team so they can check the sender and block it for everyone. One important thing: if you or anyone you know clicked a link in it or entered a password, contact the help desk right away so we can secure the account.",
  "internal_note": "KB-008. User 5 is active, with no failed logins. Her quarantine holds Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example, a lookalike domain using a capital I for the l. Subject: 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-10 21:00 UTC. It's flagged as phishing and can't be released. I did not release it. The user didn't say she clicked anything, so I didn't apply KB-029. She was told to report right away if she or anyone else did. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1) for a tenant-wide sender block and a check of other mailboxes, since she says the email is going around.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
